      "content": "The pulsing you're feeling is likely due to the stone moving, which can cause a temporary increase in blood flow to the area. To help with the pain and the pulsing, you can try applying a warm compress to the area for 15-20 minutes at a time. This can help relax the muscles and reduce discomfort. Additionally, you can try taking a combination of ibuprofen and acetaminophen, as previously mentioned. If the pulsing continues to bother you, you can also try taking a small dose of magnesium oxide, which can help relax the muscles and reduce spasms. Remember, if the pain becomes unbearable or if you experience fever, chills, or blood in your urine, you should seek medical attention immediately. But for now, just try the warm compress and pain meds, and keep drinking plenty of water to help the stone pass.",
